\caption{Derivative-band sweep for the 30 cm port arm. Narrow-band phase lag and wide-band differentiated noise compete. The deployed 15 Hz point remains close to the best measured 3-D score; it is not refitted.}\label{fig:imu-lever-arm-cutoff}
\end{figure}
}{}

The installed force is measurable even when the pooled reconstruction
penalty is small or negative. The generated results report all three axes at each offset.
A lower score can arise when the injected term opposes an existing residual;
it is not a reason to choose an incorrect sensor model.
The exact-model arm recovers the CG baseline to numerical precision.
The measured-gyro arm removes most of the installed acceleration, but its
remaining differentiated noise and lag do not guarantee a better score
for every record. The lever vector and body convention must therefore be
specified explicitly when interpreting an installation study.
